  "id": "r190cc-b-tidal-arched-spatial-rift",
  "title": "TIDAL ARCHED RIFT — inhabited sky arch and interlocking lateral void",
  "designIntent": {
    "spatialExperience": "A low metropolitan hall curls into an inhabited inclined upper arch, with one dramatic oblique void crossing the central high-rise instead of repeating decorative ribs. Public terraces and a sideways sky-dining mass remain volumetric rather than planes.",
    "silhouette": "A diagonally ascending principal body is connected to a broad suspended-looking east crown by a deep living core, while the west and rear volumes change the profile from every side. Actual 3D rotated superellipsoids define the geometry.",
    "failureToAvoid": "Reject if the front becomes a common stepped tower, if the east side looks like a fat vertical box, or if the internal sky fissure is only a cosmetic window instead of a large negative architectural space."
  },
